;; SSE and SSE2 (AX5.5, AXS59 (a), AXS62 (a); from the Intel SDM vol. 1 ch. 10-11 and vol. 2 and the AMD APM vol. 4 as
;; references): the 128-bit XMM forms of the moves, the logic, the shuffles and unpacks, the packed integer operations, the
;; scalar and packed single and double arithmetic, comparisons, minimum and maximum, square roots and the conversions, MXCSR
;; (ldmxcsr, stmxcsr). The floating-point results are computed in software at round to nearest, MXCSR's six status flags with
;; them (invalid, denormal operand, divide by zero, overflow, underflow as tininess after rounding and inexact, precision):
;; Go's float64 arithmetic is IEEE 754's at round to nearest even, the inexactness by the operations' exact error terms
;; (two-sum, fused multiply-add), the tiny results' by math/big. A rounding mode other than nearest, DAZ or FTZ in MXCSR, an
;; unmasked exception, and the approximations (rcpps, rsqrtps: each vendor's own tables) raise SIGILL as :unimplemented (AX8).
;; The MMX forms (an MM register) are unimplemented with the x87 (AX6).

(go/const
  ^{:line 20} [^{:val 1} mxIE (<< 1 0)]
  ^{:line 21} [^{:val 2} mxDE (<< 1 1)]
  ^{:line 22} [^{:val 4} mxZE (<< 1 2)]
  ^{:line 23} [^{:val 8} mxOE (<< 1 3)]
  ^{:line 24} [^{:val 16} mxUE (<< 1 4)]
  ^{:line 25} [^{:val 32} mxPE (<< 1 5)]
  ^{:line 26} [^{:val 64} mxDAZ (<< 1 6)]
  ^{:line 27} [^{:val 24576} mxRC (<< 3 13)]
  ^{:line 28} [^{:val 32768} mxFTZ (<< 1 15)]

  ^{:line 30} [^{:val 65535 :doc "MXCSRMask is the model's MXCSR_MASK: the sixteen low bits (DAZ supported, no misaligned-SSE mode)\n"} MXCSRMask 0xffff])


